\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 The Digest\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kellen Browning, Michael Corkery and Cecilia Kang \par \uc2 508 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 November 2021\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TECHNOLOGY\par \par \uc2 Activision Workers Protest\par \par \uc2 Over Misconduct Claims\par \par \uc2 A group of workers at \uc2 Activision Blizzard\uc2 , the maker of well-known video games like Call of Duty, called for the company's chief executive, \uc2 Bobby Kotick\uc2 , to step down on Tuesday because of accusations that he did not respond to claims of sexual misconduct from employees.\par \par \uc2 More than 100 employees protested at the company's studio in Irvine, Calif., on Tuesday. Many voiced their anger on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , using the hashtag #firebobbykotick.\par \par \uc2 Workers had staged a similar walkout in July after a lawsuit by a California employment agency accused \uc2 Activision\uc2  of fostering a culture of pervasive sexual harassment against women.\par \par \uc2 A Wall Street Journal article published on Tuesday morning said Mr. Kotick, who has led the gaming publisher since 2008, had known for years about complaints of sexual harassment and assault that women had brought against various men at the company, and had not taken action.\par \par \uc2 KELLEN BROWNING\par \par \uc2 EARNINGS\par \par \uc2 Walmart Beats Forecasts\par \par \uc2 With 9.2% Sales Growth\par \par \uc2 In a difficult retail environment of rising prices and snarled supply chains, \uc2 Walmart\uc2  said on Tuesday that its third-quarter sales rose and earnings topped Wall Street's expectations.\par \par \uc2 The giant retailer reported that its sales in the United States grew 9.2 percent while total revenue rose 4.3 percent to $140.5 billion.\par \par \uc2 Walmart\uc2  reported earnings per share of $1.45, beating the $1.40 that many analysts had been expecting. The better-than-expected earnings were driven by continued growth in the company's grocery and e-commerce business and its strategy of keeping prices low as consumers face inflation in just about every category of spending, from food to fuel. \uc2 Walmart\uc2 's shares were up about 1 percent in premarket trading.\par \par \uc2 In recent months, the company began chartering its own ships to circumnavigate the shipping congestion and has been pushing to hire 150,000 additional workers ahead of the holidays.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL CORKERY\par \par \uc2 REGULATORY\par \par \uc2 Senate Confirms Kanter\par \par \uc2 To Top Antitrust Position\par \par \uc2 The Senate on Tuesday confirmed \uc2 Jonathan Kanter\uc2 , a corporate lawyer and Big Tech critic, to the top antitrust role in the nation, the latest action in efforts to curb the power of Silicon Valley giants.\par \par \uc2 In a 68-to-29 vote, the approval of Mr. Kanter to lead the \uc2 Justice Department's antitrust division\uc2  filled a key position in the Biden administration. The White House has made clear that it wants to rein in consolidation in American business, especially among powerful tech companies.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Kanter has fought \uc2 Google\uc2  and other tech giants for years -- mostly as a lawyer representing rivals such as \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 , Uber, \uc2 Yelp\uc2  and \uc2 News Corp\uc2 . He joins other prominent critics of Silicon Valley in government roles, including Lina Khan, the chair of the Federal Trade Commission, who gained notoriety after writing a paper in law school arguing an antitrust theory against \uc2 Amazon\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Together, the two antitrust enforcers will lead landmark cases against \uc2 Google\uc2  and \uc2 Facebook\uc2 . CECILIA KANG\par \par \uc2 (PHOTOGRAPH BY JUSTIN SULLIVAN/GETTY IMAGES) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020211117ehbh00054\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
