\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 Netflix Workers Plan Virtual Protest Over Chappelle Program\b0\par\par\uc2 By John Koblin \par \uc2 895 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 October 2021\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The virtual walkout planned for Wednesday is the latest example of how the internal backlash over the comedian's new special has roiled the streaming service.\par \par \uc2 Two weeks after the debut of Dave Chappelle's standup special ''The Closer'' on \uc2 Netflix\uc2 , the streaming giant is still grappling with internal backlash as a group of its workers prepare to stage a virtual walkout and a former employee spoke publicly about being fired recently.\par \par \uc2 The walkout, planned for Wednesday, is the latest episode of employee unrest surrounding the special, leading to the kind of tough news coverage normally aimed at other tech companies like \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and \uc2 Google\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Many on \uc2 Netflix\uc2 's staff were angered by Mr. Chappelle's special, criticizing it as transphobic and harmful to transgender people. \uc2 Reed Hastings\uc2  and \uc2 Ted Sarandos\uc2 , \uc2 Netflix\uc2 's chief executives, have been steadfast in their support of Mr. Chappelle in communications with staff, and have argued that his special has been popular with subscribers and would not lead to real-world harm.\par \par \uc2 Netflix\uc2  also fired a worker last week for ''sharing confidential, commercially sensitive information outside the company.'' That information was included in a report by Bloomberg that included budget totals for Mr. Chappelle's specials as well as internal metrics that showed how valuable the specials were relative to their budgets.\par \par \uc2 B. Pagels-Minor, a former program manager at Netflix who is transgender, acknowledged being the fired worker in an interview on Tuesday. Laurie Burgess, a lawyer representing Mx. Pagels-Minor, who prefers a gender-neutral courtesy title and pronouns, said, ''B. categorically denies leaking sensitive information to the press.''\par \par \uc2 In a statement, a Netflix spokesperson said on Tuesday that ''while we would never normally talk about an investigation like this,'' the company contends that ''this employee admitted sharing confidential information externally from their \uc2 Netflix\uc2  email on several occasions.'' The statement added that ''they were the only employee to access detailed, sensitive data on four titles that later appeared in the press.''\par \par \uc2 Mx. Pagels-Minor, 36, said in the interview that they found last week's memos from Mr. Sarandos ''very dismissive.''\par \par \uc2 ''The tone of the message was basically like: You employees can't possibly understand the nuance of comedy, and that's why you're upset,'' Mx. Pagels-Minor said. ''That's not the point. It's not that we don't understand comedy. It's that this comedy has tones of hatred. And what are we going to do to mitigate that?''\par \par \uc2 Mx. Pagels-Minor was a leader of both the transgender and Black employee resource groups at \uc2 Netflix\uc2 . Additionally, they have been featured in promotional \uc2 Netflix\uc2  videos celebrating the diversity of the staff, with titles like ''Netflix Employees Celebrating Pride'' and ''Netflix Employees Explain What Being Black Means to Them.''\par \par \uc2 Mx. Pagels-Minor, who is 33 weeks pregnant, said they were one of the organizers of the walkout. Within hours of posting about the walkout on Thursday in a company Slack channel, Mx. Pagels-Minor said, they heard from their manager. Mx. Pagels-Minor was fired that day.\par \par \uc2 ''I don't have any ill will toward \uc2 Netflix\uc2 ,'' they said. ''I want them to be successful, but the only way to succeed is to hold themselves to the values they expound.''\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday morning, a rally is scheduled for outside \uc2 Netflix\uc2 's Los Angeles headquarters as ''a kickoff'' to the walkout, according to a social media post announcing the protest. The rally will include activists and public figures, and a ''list of firm asks'' will be sent to Mr. Sarandos, according to the post.\par \par \uc2 A Netflix software engineer, Terra Field, wrote a blog post on Medium on Monday detailing her ''whirlwind'' experience since posting a viral \uc2 Twitter\uc2  thread on Oct. 6 that said Mr. Chappelle's special ''attacks the trans community, and the very validity of transness.''\par \par \uc2 In the post, Ms. Field, who is transgender, said she was not asking that ''The Closer'' be removed from \uc2 Netflix\uc2 . Rather, she hoped executives would take concrete actions, including to ''stop pretending that transphobia in media has no effect on society.'' Ms. Field said she hoped \uc2 Netflix\uc2  would attach a warning to ''The Closer'' and other series on the streaming service that have been criticized as transphobic, and to promote ''other queer and trans content after people consume that content.''\par \par \uc2 Of ''The Closer,'' Ms. Field wrote: ''It doesn't feel good to have been working at the company that put it out there. Especially when we've spent years building out the company's policies and benefits so that it would be a great place for trans people to work.\par \par \uc2 ''A place can't be a great place to work if someone has to betray their community to do so,'' she added.\par \par \uc2 There have already been several moments of tension between rank-and-file \uc2 Netflix\uc2  employees and top executives in recent days. At an emotional companywide meeting on Friday, several staff members asked tough and persistent questions of Mr. Sarandos about the special and the company's response to the criticism of it.\par \par \uc2 Nicole Sperling contributed reporting.\par \par \uc2 Nicole Sperling contributed reporting.\par \par \uc2 Many Netflix workers called Dave Chappelle's special ''The Closer'' transphobic. A rally is set for outside Netflix's Los Angeles headquarters on Wednesday. (PHOTOGRAPH BY ROBYN BECK/AGENCE FRANCE-PRESSE, VIA GETTY IMAGES) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020211020ehak0004j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
