\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 AT&T\uc2  Expands Mandate To Most Union Workers\b0\par\par\uc2 By Noam Scheiber \par \uc2 307 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 September 2021\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The mandate will apply to tens of thousands of employees who are members of the \uc2 Communications Workers of America\uc2  union.\par \par \uc2 AT&T\uc2  announced on Wednesday that it was extending its coronavirus vaccination requirement to tens of thousands of employees who are members of the \uc2 Communications Workers of America\uc2  union.\par \par \uc2 Unionized workers who enter work locations and client or customer sites, or who are temporarily working from home, must be fully vaccinated by Feb. 1 unless they qualify for an accommodation, the company said. \uc2 AT&T\uc2  did not provide details on the exemptions.\par \par \uc2 The company had previously required that most managers be vaccinated by Oct. 11.\par \par \uc2 AT&T\uc2  held negotiations with the communications workers union over the new policy this month. A union official who was not authorized to discuss the details said the company had made a handful of concessions, including pushing back the vaccination deadline and granting employees who don't get vaccinated before the deadline an unpaid reconsideration period. But the union official said that the two sides had later reached an impasse and that the company had imposed the policy on its own.\par \par \uc2 The company did not immediately respond to a request for comment about the bargaining.\par \par \uc2 AT&T\uc2  had about 230,000 employees as of Jan. 31, according to its most recent annual report, of which about 37 percent were unionized. It operates the only major wireless carrier that is heavily unionized. A large majority of unionized employees are represented by the communications workers union.\par \par \uc2 AT&T said unionized workers who entered work locations and client or customer sites, or who were temporarily working from home, must be fully vaccinated by Feb. 1 with few exceptions. (PHOTOGRAPH BY Emily Elconin for The New York Times FOR THE NEW YORK TIMES) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020210930eh9u0003k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
