\par\par \uc2 SHOPPING GUIDE\par \uc2 Real Estate Desk; SECTRE\par \b \uc2 More Than a Way To Separate Space\b0\par\par\uc2 By Tim McKeough \par \uc2 449 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 September 2021\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 6\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 If you don't own a folding screen and you're working from home, you may want to get one. Here's why.\par \par \uc2 A folding screen is useful for dividing space, but it can do so much more.\par \par \uc2 ''It really is a great way to bring in scale, texture, artistry or a decorative moment,'' said Thom Filicia, the New York-based interior designer.\par \par \uc2 Screens, he noted, are essentially pop-up architecture.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Filicia uses them to separate various seating areas in one big space, or to soften the corners of a room. He uses them to hide ugly heating and air-conditioning equipment, and to frame or emphasize furniture, mirrors and art. And he has used them to create privacy in glass-walled apartments.\par \par \uc2 While room dividers were once de rigueur in professionally designed interiors, they are a little less common today. But Mr. Filicia thinks they're due for a pandemic-driven comeback.\par \par \uc2 ''Now that everyone's doing home offices, I think screens are really going to go through a renaissance,'' he said, because they're an ideal way to create some physical separation between work and leisure. ''Our personal spaces are becoming more multifunctional.''\par \par \uc2 How tall should a room divider be? That depends on where you plan to use it. Tall screens can be impressive, but Mr. Filicia has used screens as low as 30 inches high to conceal vents beneath a window.\par \par \uc2 Is an upholstered screen a good idea? It's an opportunity to use fabric with a beautiful texture or pattern, Mr. Filicia said, and it can also improve the acoustics of an echoey room.\par \par \uc2 Should a room divider be opaque? If the goal is complete privacy, yes, but semitransparent screens are often a better choice. ''They're sort of like lingerie for the room,'' Mr. Filicia said. ''You're seeing through them, but you're not seeing everything.''\par \par \uc2 Betty Room Divider Screen\par \par \uc2 Upholstered screen with panels of different sizes\par \par \uc2 $640 at \uc2 ABC Carpet & Home\uc2 : 646-602-3101 or abchome.com\par \par \uc2 Blink Screen\par \par \uc2 Steel screen with mirrored panels by Yabu Pushelberg\par \par \uc2 $2,200 at Stellar Works: 646-606-3760 or stellarworks.com\par \par \uc2 Roma Room Divider Screen\par \par \uc2 Iron screen with woven banana-leaf panels\par \par \uc2 $349 at \uc2 Urban Outfitters\uc2 : 800-282-2200 or urbanoutfitters.com\par \par \uc2 Anaise Cane Room Divider Screen\par \par \uc2 Black-stained wood-and-cane screen with arched panels\par \par \uc2 $549 at \uc2 Crate & Barrel\uc2 : 800-967-6696 or crateandbarrel.com\par \par \uc2 Venier Screen\par \par \uc2 Leather-and-metal screen by Sebastian Herkner\par \par \uc2 About $7,700 at \uc2 1stdibs\uc2 : \uc2 1stdibs.com\par \par \uc2 For weekly email updates on residential real estate news, sign up here. Follow us on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : @nytrealestate.\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020210912eh9c00031\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
